# .trivyignore for the idp-portal (Backstage) container image.
#
# ─── POLICY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same convention as platform-hello/.trivyignore (Phase 7 bug #3):
#   - Only CVEs we deliberately tolerate get listed here
#   - Every entry needs a REASON + a REVIEW DATE
#   - Trivy still prints these on every CI run (gitleaks-style visibility)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ─── CONTEXT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backstage pulls in ~1700 transitive deps; a handful always carry
# open CVEs. The 8W3.3 sweep (2026-11-19) fixed everything fixable
# without a major-version jump:
#   - yarn up -R for in-range stale resolutions
#     (node-forge 1.4.3, follow-redirects 1.16.3, undici 7.30.2/8.12.4,
#      markdown-it 14.3.3, body-parser 1.20.9/2.4.0, multer 2.5.0)
#   - yarn resolutions for out-of-range requests
#     (undici exact-pin 7.29.0 → ^7.30.1)
#   - base-image CVEs (zlib1g) died with the 8W3.2 Wolfi swap
#   - 12 stale blocks (tar, brace-expansion, picomatch, sigstore,
#     pacote, ip-address, zod, ...) had already been fixed by normal
#     dependency drift — verified gone via local Trivy fs scan of
#     yarn.lock, which is a SUPERSET of the image scan (image strips
#     devDeps), then pruned.
#
# What remains falls in exactly two buckets:
#   1. Fix requires a major-version jump of a transitive we don't
#      control (undici 5→6 under urllib@3) — tolerated with mitigation
#      until the owning @backstage package line moves
#   2. Fix requires bumping the @backstage framework line itself —
#      that's a dedicated Backstage-upgrade task, not a resolutions
#      patch (resolutions on framework packages break plugin wiring)
#
# Review cycle: WEEKLY (7-day). Re-run the local scan
#   (docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/scan" aquasec/trivy fs \
#      --scanners vuln --severity HIGH,CRITICAL /scan)
# against portal/; remove entries that no longer appear.
# Next review: 2026-11-26

# ─── CVEs: @backstage/backend-defaults ──────────────────────────────
# Access control bypass via improper service credential delegation.
# Fix: @backstage/backend-defaults >= 0.17.8. The tree holds BOTH
# 0.17.8+ (our backend) and an old 0.12.3 copy pinned by an older
# plugin's dependency range — the flagged copy is the 0.12.3 one.
# Mitigation: since Phase 8 Wave 1 all requests pass GitHub OAuth
# (guest provider inert); the delegation bypass needs an
# authenticated foothold first. Real fix is the Backstage framework
# bump (dedicated upgrade task).
CVE-2026-106492

# ─── CVEs: @fastify/busboy ──────────────────────────────────────────
# DoS from crafted form-data headers. Fix: 3.2.1 (we're on 2.1.1,
# major jump). Mitigation: Backstage's form endpoints are all behind
# GitHub OAuth since Wave 1.
CVE-2026-19481

# ─── CVEs: @graphql-tools/utils ─────────────────────────────────────
# DoS via prototype pollution in mergeDeep. Fix: 12.0.1 (we're on
# 8.13.1, 4-major jump). Mitigation: Backstage doesn't expose GraphQL
# mutations to anonymous traffic; mergeDeep is only reached via
# internal API calls.
CVE-2026-104852

# ─── CVEs: basic-ftp ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DoS via crafted Unix directory listings. Fix: 6.2.1 (we're on
# 5.3.1, major jump). Mitigation: Backstage doesn't initiate FTP from
# user input.
CVE-2026-102990

# ─── CVEs: undici (5.x line only, under urllib@3) ───────────────────
# 5 CVEs against undici 5.29.0: unbounded-memory DoS (CVE-2026-12151,
# CVE-2026-1526), invalid-WebSocket DoS (CVE-2026-2229), certificate
# validation bypass via dropped options (CVE-2026-109383), TLS
# renegotiation DoS (CVE-2026-87018). No fixed 5.x release exists —
# fixes start at 6.27.0/6.29.1, a major jump under urllib@3 (built
# for undici 5 APIs), itself pinned by the old
# @backstage/backend-defaults@0.12.3 copy (see CVE-2026-106492).
# The 8W3.3 sweep moved every OTHER undici line to patched versions
# (7.30.2 / 8.12.4); this is the single remaining vulnerable copy.
# Mitigation: undici here is an internal in-cluster HTTP client
# (K8s API, GitHub API) — not reached by untrusted input; the
# cert-validation bypass only applies to Backstage calling OUT to
# known-good endpoints. Dies with the Backstage framework bump.
CVE-2026-12151
CVE-2026-1526
CVE-2026-2229
CVE-2026-109383
CVE-2026-87018

# ─── CVEs: urllib ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credential leakage via cross-origin redirects. Fix: 4.9.1 — also in
# the tree; the flagged copy is urllib@3.27.3 under the old
# backend-defaults@0.12.3 (same root cause as the undici 5.x block).
# Mitigation: Backstage doesn't follow user-controlled redirects.
CVE-2026-55553

# ─── CVEs: @azure/msal-node ─────────────────────────────────────────
# MSAL Node authorization code flow may disclose parameters to third
# parties. Fix: 7.1.0 (we're on 6.0.1, major jump). Mitigation:
# msal-node is transitively pulled by the Azure auth module which we
# don't configure — Azure OAuth is not in our providers list.
CVE-2026-109461
